  {:id       :verify-cljs-runner-completeness
   :title    "ClojureScript test runners that run less than the suite they sit in"
   :why      "ADR-2608170200 moves :jvm-test fleet gates to :nbb-test, and the :nbb-test
              gate's own floor only requires that SOME `Ran N tests` line appear. A runner
              covering a third of its suite satisfies that floor, so a gate can be moved
              to a cheaper node and silently stop testing most of its subject with an
              identical signed receipt. Measured on kotoba-lang/columnar before its
              repair: `clojure -M:test` ran 36 tests / 117 assertions, `nbb test/run.cljs`
              ran 10 / 54, and with group/group deliberately broken the partial runner
              printed `Ran 10 tests ... 0 failures` and exited 0. Nothing prints the
              number it should have reached, which is why only a detector can see it.
              What it has already caught beyond columnar: kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer ships
              17 `_test.cljc` and 2 `_test.cljs`; its nbb runner auto-discovers
              `_test.cljc` only, so those two namespaces run under shadow-cljs
              (`:ns-regexp \"-test$\"`) and never under nbb -- while the runner's own
              docstring calls itself a genuine third platform tier. No other check in the
              workspace compares a runner against the tree it sits in."
   :argv     ["nbb" "--classpath" "{{repo}}:{{repo}}/scripts/nbb_compat"
              "{{repo}}/scripts/verify-cljs-runner-completeness.cljs" "--findings"]
   :cwd      :root
   :findings :protocol
   :evidence "SCANNED\t[1-9][0-9]*\t"
